My former Cambridge
colleagues Teresa Shawcross and Richard Payne have also provided
much inspiration and assistance through their own work;

Emperors
had long felt under a duty to settle religious disputes amongst their
subjects;

It was to address this new
and formidable foe that Khusro had been obliged to withdraw from
Lazica;

The defeat of the Gepid king in 567 was thus to a great extent a victory
of Byzantine diplomacy: the Avars had seemingly been weaned off
imperial subsidy;

Constantine Lardys, the former praetorian prefect, logothete,
and curator of the palace of Hormisdas, and Theodosius the [remaining]
son of Maurice were slain at Diadromoi, near Acritas;

In such circumstances, the army could barely be relied upon even
for the defence of Anatolia and the land approaches to Constantinople,
let alone an aggressive campaign to regain lost ground.

